  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Helaman",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 11,
    "summary": "Nephi persuades the Lord to replace their war with a famine—Many people perish—They repent, and Nephi importunes the Lord for rain—Nephi and Lehi receive many revelations—The Gadianton robbers entrench themselves in the land. About 20–6 B.C.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "And now it came to pass in the seventy and second year of the reign of the judges that the contentions did increase, insomuch that there were wars throughout all the land among all the people of Nephi.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Helaman 11:1",
        "book": "Helaman",
        "chapter": 11,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "And it was this secret band of robbers who did carry on this work of destruction and wickedness. And this war did last all that year; and in the seventy and third year it did also last.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 22,
            "text": "Hel. 6:22 (18–24); 11:26 (25–26)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Helaman 11:2",
        "book": "Helaman",
        "chapter": 11,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that in this year Nephi did cry unto the Lord, saying:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Helaman 11:3",
        "book": "Helaman",
        "chapter": 11,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "O Lord, do not suffer that this people shall be destroyed by the sword; but O Lord, rather let there be a famine in the land, to stir them up in remembrance of the Lord their God, and perhaps they will repent and turn unto thee.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 91,
            "end": 94,
            "text": "Hel. 11:14."
          },
          {
            "start": 106,
            "end": 112,
            "text": "1 Kgs. 8:35; 1 Chr. 21:12; Hel. 10:6. TG Famine."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Hel. 11:14.",
            "prettyString": "Helaman 11:14",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "helaman",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 11,
                    "end": 11,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 14,
                        "end": 14
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Helaman 11:4",
        "book": "Helaman",
        "chapter": 11,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "And so it was done, according to the words of Nephi. And there was a great famine upon the land, among all the people of Nephi. And thus in the seventy and fourth year the famine did continue, and the work of destruction did cease by the sword but became sore by famine.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Helaman 11:5",
        "book": "Helaman",
        "chapter": 11,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "And this work of destruction did also continue in the seventy and fifth year. For the earth was smitten that it was dry, and did not yield forth grain in the season of grain; and the whole earth was smitten, even among the Lamanites as well as among the Nephites, so that they were smitten that they did perish by thousands in the more wicked parts of the land.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 116,
            "end": 119,
            "text": "TG Drought."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Drought.",
            "prettyString": "TG Drought",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Drought",
                "entryId": "tg-drought",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Helaman 11:6",
        "book": "Helaman",
        "chapter": 11,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that the people saw that they were about to perish by famine, and they began to remember the Lord their God; and they began to remember the words of Nephi.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 100,
            "end": 108,
            "text": "Amos 4:7 (6–10); Hel. 12:3."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Helaman 11:7",
        "book": "Helaman",
        "chapter": 11,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "And the people began to plead with their chief judges and their leaders, that they would say unto Nephi: Behold, we know that thou art a man of God, and therefore cry unto the Lord our God that he turn away from us this famine, lest all the words which thou hast spoken concerning our destruction be fulfilled.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 20,
            "text": "Ex. 10:7."
          },
          {
            "start": 285,
            "end": 296,
            "text": "Hel. 10:11 (11–14)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Ex. 10:7.",
            "prettyString": "Exodus 10:7",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "exodus",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 10,
                    "end": 10,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 7,
                        "end": 7
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Helaman 11:8",
        "book": "Helaman",
        "chapter": 11,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that the judges did say unto Nephi, according to the words which had been desired. And it came to pass that when Nephi saw that the people had repented and did humble themselves in sackcloth, he cried again unto the Lord, saying:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 163,
            "end": 171,
            "text": "Morm. 2:12."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Morm. 2:12.",
            "prettyString": "Mormon 2:12",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "mormon",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 2,
                    "end": 2,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 12,
                        "end": 12
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Helaman 11:9",
        "book": "Helaman",
        "chapter": 11,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "O Lord, behold this people repenteth; and they have swept away the band of Gadianton from amongst them insomuch that they have become extinct, and they have concealed their secret plans in the earth.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Helaman 11:10",
        "book": "Helaman",
        "chapter": 11,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "Now, O Lord, because of this their humility wilt thou turn away thine anger, and let thine anger be appeased in the destruction of those wicked men whom thou hast already destroyed.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Helaman 11:11",
        "book": "Helaman",
        "chapter": 11,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "O Lord, wilt thou turn away thine anger, yea, thy fierce anger, and cause that this famine may cease in this land.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Helaman 11:12",
        "book": "Helaman",
        "chapter": 11,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "O Lord, wilt thou hearken unto me, and cause that it may be done according to my words, and send forth rain upon the face of the earth, that she may bring forth her fruit, and her grain in the season of grain.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 103,
            "end": 107,
            "text": "1 Kgs. 18:41 (1, 41–46)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Helaman 11:13",
        "book": "Helaman",
        "chapter": 11,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "O Lord, thou didst hearken unto my words when I said, Let there be a famine, that the pestilence of the sword might cease; and I know that thou wilt, even at this time, hearken unto my words, for thou saidst that: If this people repent I will spare them.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 32,
            "end": 40,
            "text": "Hel. 11:4."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Hel. 11:4.",
            "prettyString": "Helaman 11:4",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "helaman",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 11,
                    "end": 11,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 4,
                        "end": 4
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Helaman 11:14",
        "book": "Helaman",
        "chapter": 11,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "Yea, O Lord, and thou seest that they have repented, because of the famine and the pestilence and destruction which has come unto them.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Helaman 11:15",
        "book": "Helaman",
        "chapter": 11,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "And now, O Lord, wilt thou turn away thine anger, and try again if they will serve thee? And if so, O Lord, thou canst bless them according to thy words which thou hast said.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Helaman 11:16",
        "book": "Helaman",
        "chapter": 11,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that in the seventy and sixth year the Lord did turn away his anger from the people, and caused that rain should fall upon the earth, insomuch that it did bring forth her fruit in the season of her fruit. And it came to pass that it did bring forth her grain in the season of her grain.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 121,
            "end": 125,
            "text": "Deut. 11:14 (13–17); Ether 2:24; D&C 117:1."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Helaman 11:17",
        "book": "Helaman",
        "chapter": 11,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "And behold, the people did rejoice and glorify God, and the whole face of the land was filled with rejoicing; and they did no more seek to destroy Nephi, but they did esteem him as a great prophet, and a man of God, having great power and authority given unto him from God.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 183,
            "end": 188,
            "text": "Hel. 10:7 (5–11)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Helaman 11:18",
        "book": "Helaman",
        "chapter": 11,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "And behold, Lehi, his brother, was not a whit behind him as to things pertaining to righteousness.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 45,
            "text": "Hel. 5:44 (36–44); 6:6."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Helaman 11:19",
        "book": "Helaman",
        "chapter": 11,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "And thus it did come to pass that the people of Nephi began to prosper again in the land, and began to build up their waste places, and began to multiply and spread, even until they did cover the whole face of the land, both on the northward and on the southward, from the sea west to the sea east.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 186,
            "end": 191,
            "text": "Jarom 1:6; Alma 22:27 (27, 32–33); Hel. 3:8; 3 Ne. 1:17."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Helaman 11:20",
        "book": "Helaman",
        "chapter": 11,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that the seventy and sixth year did end in peace. And the seventy and seventh year began in peace; and the church did spread throughout the face of all the land; and the more part of the people, both the Nephites and the Lamanites, did belong to the church; and they did have exceedingly great peace in the land; and thus ended the seventy and seventh year.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 127,
            "end": 133,
            "text": "TG Church; Peace."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Church; Peace.",
            "prettyString": "TG Church; TG Peace",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Church",
                "entryId": "tg-church",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              },
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Peace",
                "entryId": "tg-peace",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Helaman 11:21",
        "book": "Helaman",
        "chapter": 11,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "And also they had peace in the seventy and eighth year, save it were a few contentions concerning the points of doctrine which had been laid down by the prophets.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Helaman 11:22",
        "book": "Helaman",
        "chapter": 11,
        "verse": 22
      },
      {
        "text": "And in the seventy and ninth year there began to be much strife. But it came to pass that Nephi and Lehi, and many of their brethren who knew concerning the true points of doctrine, having many revelations daily, therefore they did preach unto the people, insomuch that they did put an end to their strife in that same year.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 194,
            "end": 205,
            "text": "Jarom 1:4; Alma 26:22; D&C 107:19."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 23,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Jarom 1:4; Alma 26:22; D&C 107:19.",
            "prettyString": "Jarom 1:4; Alma 26:22; D&C 107:19",
